  "part": 3,
  "level": "A2",
  "title": "The perfect tenses",
  "tagline": "He comido, había llegado: haber + participle, and how Latin America and Spain use them.",
  "goal": "Form the present perfect and the past perfect, use irregular participles, and know when Latin Americans prefer the preterite.",
  "minutes": 10,
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "formas",
      "title": "Haber + participle",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "conjugation",
          "persons": ["yo", "tú", "él / ella / usted", "nosotros", "ellos / ellas / ustedes"],
          "verbs": [
            { "verb": "present perfect", "meaning": "I have eaten", "forms": ["{he} comido", "{has} comido", "{ha} comido", "{hemos} comido", "{han} comido"] },
            { "verb": "past perfect", "meaning": "I had eaten", "forms": ["{había} comido", "{habías} comido", "{había} comido", "{habíamos} comido", "{habían} comido"] }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Participles: **-ar → -ado** (*hablado*), **-er / -ir → -ido** (*comido, vivido*). The participle **never changes** and nothing goes between *haber* and it: *Nunca he estado* (never «he nunca estado»)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "irregulares",
      "title": "Irregular participles",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "table",
          "head": ["Verb", "Participle", "Verb", "Participle"],
          "rows": [
            ["*hacer*", "*hecho*", "*decir*", "*dicho*"],
            ["*ver*", "*visto*", "*escribir*", "*escrito*"],
            ["*poner*", "*puesto*", "*volver*", "*vuelto*"],
            ["*abrir*", "*abierto*", "*romper*", "*roto*"],
            ["*morir*", "*muerto*", "*devolver*", "*devuelto*"]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "usos",
      "title": "When to use them",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "table",
          "head": ["Tense", "Use", "Example"],
          "rows": [
            ["Present perfect", "Life experience (*alguna vez, nunca*), things not finished yet (*ya, todavía no*)", "*¿{Has estado} en Perú? Todavía no {he comido}.*"],
            ["Past perfect", "Something that had happened before another past moment", "*Cuando llegué, ya {habían cenado}.*"]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "tone": "note",
          "title": "Latin America vs Spain",
          "text": "For something that happened today, Spain uses the present perfect (*Hoy {he comido} paella*) and most of Latin America the preterite (*Hoy {comí} paella*). Both are understood everywhere."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
